<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bengal Army</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> Army was the army of the Bengal Presidency of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> and later of the British Crown, the largest of the three presidency armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Its high-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">caste</a> sepoys from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awadh">Awadh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> formed the core of the rebellion of 1857, which began at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meerut">Meerut</a>. After the rising it was rebuilt with recruits from other groups, and in 1895 it was merged into the unified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-army">Indian Army</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bengal-army.jpg" alt="Bengal Army" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Yaddah assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_British_East_India_Company_(1801).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
